# Offline pin notes — gpw-mbd-hirshfeld

## Method

Hirshfeld \(V/V_{\mathrm{free}}\) from the GPW PBE valence density (in-tree
exponential free-atom model, `hirshfeld_tables.h`) → MBD@rsSCS with scaled
α/C6/R (same libMBD free-atom tables as `gpw-mbd-ice`).

## Why not stock CP2K QS?

CP2K 2026.1 `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` is only DFTD2|DFTD3|DFTD3(BJ)|DFTD4 — no
stock TS/MBD. Hosts may link libMBD externally. Hard pin:

1. Dual pure-Python Hirshfeld on the same free-atom exponential model
   (unit-test `SuperpositionGivesUnitVolumeRatios` + grid integral).
2. libMBD / ATV `mbd_rsscs_pbe` energy with those volume ratios
   (free-atom MBD already pinned vs libMBD Fortran git `88069c6`).

Geometry: same water dimer as `gpw-mbd-ice` / `gpw-ts-ice`.

## Free-atom model (document for dual)

```
rho_Z(r) = A exp(-alpha r),  A = N_val * alpha^3 / (8 pi)
V_free   = 60 * N_val / alpha^3
H: N=1, alpha=2.0 ; O: N=6, alpha=2.2  (compact valence-like)
```

See `include/atomiverse/cpu/gpw/basis_data/hirshfeld_tables.h`.

## Pin (product settings)

```
E_disp = -1.1479852469005181e-03 Ha
volumes (O H H O H H) ≈ 0.7403 0.6529 0.6529 0.7153 0.5784 0.5784
CUTOFF 200 Ry, DZVP-MOLOPT-SR-GTH, GTH-PBE, water dimer 12 Å cell
```
